1
00:02:12,065 --> 00:02:13,293
Damn it!

2
00:02:20,773 --> 00:02:21,762
Rear armor?

3
00:02:21,875 --> 00:02:22,864
Shot to hell.

4
00:02:25,011 --> 00:02:26,007
You better
drop back...

5
00:02:26,112 --> 00:02:28,842
It's the last lap.
We can win this.

6
00:02:28,948 --> 00:02:31,644
Why don't this son
of a bitch just die?

7
00:02:32,318 --> 00:02:33,376
Oil.

8
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:35,478
Out.

9
00:02:37,123 --> 00:02:38,249
Smoke.

10
00:02:39,058 --> 00:02:40,355
Finished.

11
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:42,555
Give me the napalm!

12
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:44,152
Nothing works!

13
00:02:48,501 --> 00:02:50,662
Drop the tombstone.

14
00:02:50,770 --> 00:02:52,738
On my mark. Three,

15
00:02:54,641 --> 00:02:55,733
two,

16
00:02:56,809 --> 00:02:57,798
one.

17
00:02:57,911 --> 00:03:00,072
I got you now,
motherfucker.

18
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:02,140
Mark!

19
00:03:04,717 --> 00:03:05,843
Shit!

20
00:03:07,554 --> 00:03:08,680
Fuck!

21
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:13,118
That's how you want
to do it? Okay.

22
00:03:26,773 --> 00:03:29,503
He's still coming.
Our tank is exposed.

23
00:03:30,810 --> 00:03:33,278
He's got us, Frank.
You have to drop back.

24
00:03:33,846 --> 00:03:36,974
It's a quarter mile to
the line. I can make it.

25
00:03:41,387 --> 00:03:43,184
<i>Sayonara,</i> Frankie.

26
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:45,357
Punch out.

27
00:03:45,458 --> 00:03:46,482
I'm sorry.

28
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:53,514
Forty years.
Longer than my marriage.

29
00:05:54,954 --> 00:05:57,081
Sounds like you're
gonna miss this place.

30
00:05:57,190 --> 00:06:01,092
I still can't believe they
closed it down. Just like that.

31
00:06:02,261 --> 00:06:04,195
The only thing I'm gonna
miss is my paycheck.

32
00:06:04,297 --> 00:06:07,061
Well, it was honest
work for honest men.

33
00:06:07,633 --> 00:06:10,727
I got a family to feed,
and there's no work out there.

34
00:06:10,837 --> 00:06:13,829
I hear they might be
hiring down at the docks.

35
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:15,567
Five men, maybe.

36
00:06:16,242 --> 00:06:17,470
Hey, thanks, man.

37
00:06:17,577 --> 00:06:18,737
Thanks, Jensen.

38
00:06:32,458 --> 00:06:34,824
<i>Collect your final paycheck and leave.</i>

39
00:06:34,927 --> 00:06:38,226
<i>The main gate will be</i>
<i>locked in 15 minutes.</i>

40
00:06:44,804 --> 00:06:46,704
Get ready to be
ripped off, boys.

41
00:06:46,806 --> 00:06:50,572
<i>Collect your paycheck and leave
the premises in an orderly manner.</i>

42
00:06:50,676 --> 00:06:53,804
<i>The main gate will be</i>
<i>locked in 15 minutes.</i>

43
00:07:02,688 --> 00:07:03,985
Cash or check?

44
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:05,887
Better make it cash.

45
00:07:07,493 --> 00:07:08,790
$300.

46
00:07:09,695 --> 00:07:12,323
I worked 120 hours
the last two weeks.

47
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:14,297
Cash fee. Next!
Cash fee?

48
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,765
You wanted cash,
there's a fee.

49
00:07:15,868 --> 00:07:17,199
You want a check
instead?

50
00:07:17,303 --> 00:07:20,033
Seeing as the company's out
of business, not exactly.

51
00:07:20,139 --> 00:07:23,472
You don't like it, there's
the complaint box. Next!

52
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:37,150
They never get it.

53
00:07:38,391 --> 00:07:40,359
Self-fulfilling prophecy.

54
00:07:59,178 --> 00:08:01,578
We're honest workers.
We're just like you guys!

55
00:08:01,681 --> 00:08:04,081
What the hell are
you doing here?

56
00:08:09,388 --> 00:08:10,855
You bastards!

57
00:08:12,592 --> 00:08:14,253
Shit! Shit!
Ross!

58
00:08:15,394 --> 00:08:16,383
You okay, Ross?

59
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:18,555
Rubber bullets,
the assholes!

60
00:08:40,819 --> 00:08:41,911
Come on!

61
00:08:42,721 --> 00:08:44,154
Come on!

62
00:09:22,978 --> 00:09:23,967
Hi, honey.

63
00:09:24,079 --> 00:09:25,307
Hi. Sorry
I'm so late.

64
00:09:29,217 --> 00:09:31,082
Nice day at work?

65
00:09:31,186 --> 00:09:33,313
Yeah. Just fine.

66
00:09:37,492 --> 00:09:39,255
Give me that shirt.

67
00:09:40,996 --> 00:09:43,794
They called the riot
police. It got ugly.

68
00:09:44,366 --> 00:09:46,129
I don't deserve you.

69
00:09:48,303 --> 00:09:49,964
You're a good man,
Jensen Ames.

70
00:09:50,071 --> 00:09:53,507
And it doesn't matter what
anyone else thinks but me.

71
00:10:00,048 --> 00:10:03,211
So, $300. That's
all they gave us.

72
00:10:05,020 --> 00:10:07,420
We'll make it last.
We always do.

73
00:10:08,423 --> 00:10:10,584
I'll start
looking tomorrow.

74
00:10:12,027 --> 00:10:14,222
I think you're forgetting
that I married you

75
00:10:14,329 --> 00:10:16,627
for your
non-financial assets.

76
00:10:17,866 --> 00:10:18,833
Did you now?

77
00:10:18,934 --> 00:10:19,992
Mmm-hmm.

78
00:10:44,359 --> 00:10:48,659
Daddy's home. Is it you
who was making all that noise?

79
00:10:49,497 --> 00:10:52,125
<i>What does little</i>
<i>Piper want? Want a story?</i>

80
00:10:52,968 --> 00:10:55,402
You know you
won't understand it.

81
00:10:56,538 --> 00:10:59,132
<i>But it will be good practice for me.</i>
But it will be good practice for me.

82
00:11:07,315 --> 00:11:08,805
What the hell.

83
00:11:10,151 --> 00:11:12,051
Let's go crazy.

84
00:11:24,499 --> 00:11:26,364
Something smells good.

85
00:11:30,572 --> 00:11:31,698
Honey?

86
00:11:32,674 --> 00:11:33,902
Suzy?

87
00:11:49,891 --> 00:11:53,383
Stay on the ground!
Stay on the ground.

88
00:11:53,495 --> 00:11:56,464
Drop the knife!

89
00:11:56,564 --> 00:11:59,192
Do not resist!
Stay on the ground!

90
00:11:59,634 --> 00:12:00,601
Stay where you are!

91
00:12:00,702 --> 00:12:02,431
Stay on the ground!

92
00:12:05,707 --> 00:12:07,174
Don't move!

93
00:13:46,957 --> 00:13:48,083
Move.

94
00:13:59,803 --> 00:14:01,395
Get up against
the wall.

95
00:14:21,192 --> 00:14:22,352
Scrub yourself.

96
00:14:59,630 --> 00:15:00,597
Stop.

97
00:15:02,499 --> 00:15:04,433
Prisoner will
step back.

98
00:15:15,212 --> 00:15:16,839
Happy holidays.

99
00:16:03,894 --> 00:16:05,090
They slipped.

100
00:16:31,772 --> 00:16:33,034
Good morning.
Morning.

101
00:16:33,140 --> 00:16:34,129
Morning, Warden.

102
00:16:34,241 --> 00:16:35,230
Morning.

103
00:16:36,943 --> 00:16:37,932
Good morning, ma'am.

104
00:16:38,045 --> 00:16:39,535
Good morning.

105
00:16:40,614 --> 00:16:43,447
There goes the baddest ass in the yard.

106
00:16:43,550 --> 00:16:45,677
Sound like you're
in love, homie.

107
00:16:46,319 --> 00:16:47,411
I am.

108
00:17:00,067 --> 00:17:02,535
Damn. I had to
wake up for this?

109
00:17:07,007 --> 00:17:08,338
All right, is it
my imagination,

110
00:17:08,442 --> 00:17:10,273
or is this shit
getting worse?

111
00:17:10,377 --> 00:17:12,174
Like, what is this
supposed to be?

112
00:17:12,279 --> 00:17:13,507
Oatmeal.

113
00:17:14,614 --> 00:17:15,740
I think.

114
00:17:15,849 --> 00:17:17,544
Man, how do you
fuck up oatmeal?

115
00:17:21,354 --> 00:17:23,117
Who's the new guy?

116
00:17:23,890 --> 00:17:25,118
Jensen Ames.

117
00:17:25,225 --> 00:17:26,283
The driver?

118
00:17:26,393 --> 00:17:27,621
Never heard
of him.

119
00:17:28,295 --> 00:17:31,389
Oh, yeah, I saw him race
years ago. He's good.

120
00:17:32,099 --> 00:17:34,260
Did some time
upstate.

121
00:17:34,367 --> 00:17:35,857
Killed his career.

122
00:17:35,969 --> 00:17:39,496
Holder of the fastest laps
at Willard, Union and Butler.

123
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:43,268
I hope he's as fast off
the track as he is on.

124
00:17:59,159 --> 00:18:00,786
Never a dull day.

125
00:18:11,037 --> 00:18:13,562
Let's get the fuck
out of here.

126
00:18:18,778 --> 00:18:21,246
Heads up.
It's Pachenko.

127
00:18:33,193 --> 00:18:35,218
So you're the
wife killer.

128
00:18:36,630 --> 00:18:39,030
Takes a big man
to kill a woman.

129
00:18:43,336 --> 00:18:45,634
I suppose you
rape kiddies, too.

130
00:18:47,174 --> 00:18:49,199
You hear that,
everyone?

131
00:18:49,309 --> 00:18:52,107
Guy kills women.
Rapes kiddies.

132
00:18:54,481 --> 00:18:57,279
What do you think we
ought to do about that?

133
00:19:07,727 --> 00:19:11,026
Get down on the ground!
Down on the ground! Now!

134
00:19:11,698 --> 00:19:13,188
Nobody move!

135
00:19:16,570 --> 00:19:18,094
Nobody move!

136
00:19:22,225 --> 00:19:25,126
I guess he didn't like
the oatmeal, either.

137
00:19:33,536 --> 00:19:34,935
Well, you've
got stones.

138
00:19:35,972 --> 00:19:38,805
Putting the hurt on
a Brotherhood general.

139
00:19:39,442 --> 00:19:43,139
But right now, that's the
least of your problems.

140
00:19:44,213 --> 00:19:48,513
The warden does bad things to people
that mix it up with the drivers.

141
00:19:57,709 --> 00:20:01,008
Prisoner 77119, ma'am.

142
00:20:02,247 --> 00:20:04,181
Thank you, Mr. Ulrich.

143
00:20:05,016 --> 00:20:07,678
This prison is the
home to murderers,

144
00:20:07,786 --> 00:20:10,414
rapists and violent
offenders of every kind.

145
00:20:12,157 --> 00:20:16,491
The United States penal system
sends me the worst of the worst.

146
00:20:16,595 --> 00:20:18,893
But the men
you've provoked...

147
00:20:19,531 --> 00:20:21,726
Well, let's just
say, Mr. Ames,

148
00:20:21,833 --> 00:20:23,266
that the life term
you joined us for

149
00:20:23,368 --> 00:20:25,893
may be a lot shorter
than you think.

150
00:20:26,004 --> 00:20:27,995
I understand.
Tradition.

151
00:20:28,106 --> 00:20:31,803
Soften up the new guy.
An ass-slapping good time had by all.

152
00:20:37,549 --> 00:20:40,518
Foul language
is an issue

153
00:20:41,653 --> 00:20:42,950
for me.

154
00:20:55,066 --> 00:20:56,363
While looking
over your record,

155
00:20:56,468 --> 00:21:00,029
I couldn't help noticing
your occupational history.

156
00:21:00,338 --> 00:21:03,501
It seems you have some
talent behind the wheel.

157
00:21:07,312 --> 00:21:11,112
Out of curiosity, when was
the last time you raced?

158
00:21:11,216 --> 00:21:14,310
It's been a while.
I lost my license.

159
00:21:16,021 --> 00:21:18,012
What if I could
help you?

160
00:21:18,490 --> 00:21:19,855
Get my license back?

161
00:21:22,227 --> 00:21:24,457
I had something
else in mind.

162
00:21:26,798 --> 00:21:28,732
You're familiar
with the Death Race

163
00:21:28,834 --> 00:21:31,632
and the driver the
fans call Frankenstein?

164
00:21:32,471 --> 00:21:34,530
A man so disfigured
by crashes

165
00:21:34,639 --> 00:21:36,664
that he's forced
to wear a mask.

166
00:21:38,043 --> 00:21:41,035
His return to the track
is highly anticipated,

167
00:21:41,146 --> 00:21:43,273
and therein lies
my problem.

168
00:21:43,882 --> 00:21:46,180
No one knows yet,
but poor Frank died

169
00:21:46,284 --> 00:21:49,549
on an operating table not
long after his last race.

170
00:21:50,522 --> 00:21:52,581
Anyone can
wear the mask.

171
00:21:52,691 --> 00:21:55,319
But not just anyone
can drive the car.

172
00:21:59,698 --> 00:22:00,858
You have the skills I require
to keep the legend alive.

173
00:22:03,668 --> 00:22:06,136
I want you to become
Frankenstein.

174
00:22:07,572 --> 00:22:08,971
No, thanks.

175
00:22:10,342 --> 00:22:11,707
He's dead.

176
00:22:12,377 --> 00:22:14,868
Why don't you just
tell the truth?

177
00:22:15,914 --> 00:22:18,542
The audience wants
to see Frank again.

178
00:22:19,518 --> 00:22:22,646
He moves them.
Inspires them.

179
00:22:23,388 --> 00:22:26,721
And in this world, that's
not so easy to come by.

180
00:22:30,295 --> 00:22:32,820
What makes you
think for a second

181
00:22:33,331 --> 00:22:36,095
I would risk my life
doing this for you?

182
00:22:37,669 --> 00:22:39,330
Win five races,

183
00:22:40,071 --> 00:22:41,561
you go free.

184
00:22:42,908 --> 00:22:44,705
Those are the rules.

185
00:22:45,410 --> 00:22:47,378
And Frank
has won four.

186
00:22:48,647 --> 00:22:50,171
Win one more,

187
00:22:51,550 --> 00:22:52,949
you walk.

188
00:22:54,252 --> 00:22:56,220
Call it intuition,
but...

189
00:22:59,691 --> 00:23:01,488
I don't think you
belong in here

190
00:23:01,593 --> 00:23:03,993
with the rest
of these animals.

191
00:23:06,598 --> 00:23:08,566
I might surprise you.

192
00:23:21,296 --> 00:23:24,459
The race is Friday, and
I need your decision.

193
00:23:25,967 --> 00:23:28,629
Ten seconds from now,
I will retract this offer,

194
00:23:28,737 --> 00:23:34,107
and extend it to Prisoner
68815, James Francis Barlini,

195
00:23:34,209 --> 00:23:36,109
who, clearly not
of your caliber,

196
00:23:36,211 --> 00:23:38,042
will be quite
enthusiastic about it.

197
00:23:38,847 --> 00:23:43,875
And you, unfortunately, will need to
spend your incarceration in solitary.

198
00:23:44,619 --> 00:23:47,884
Since now I know your
dirty little secret.

199
00:23:48,190 --> 00:23:50,283
I'm sure you'll find
solitary preferable

200
00:23:50,392 --> 00:23:54,453
to what Mr. Pachenko and his
friends have in mind for you.

201
00:23:55,764 --> 00:23:58,927
You're a skilled driver.
Your chances are good.

202
00:24:00,635 --> 00:24:03,433
I'm offering you your
freedom, Mr. Ames.

203
00:24:05,207 --> 00:24:08,870
If it's not worth risking
your life for, what is?

204
00:24:23,374 --> 00:24:27,174
All right, turn her up and tighten
the lines! She's hemorrhaging!

205
00:24:30,081 --> 00:24:31,309
Ma'am.

206
00:24:31,415 --> 00:24:34,543
You don't have to call me "ma'am."
You know that.

207
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:38,912
This is Mr. Ames.
You know why he's here.

208
00:24:39,524 --> 00:24:40,991
Oh, I do now.

209
00:24:42,160 --> 00:24:44,253
The race is less
than a week away.

210
00:24:44,362 --> 00:24:46,660
I have great
confidence in you.

211
00:24:48,099 --> 00:24:51,296
Well, then, I'll leave
you two to get acquainted.

212
00:24:55,006 --> 00:24:58,601
Jensen Garner Ames.
Moved to the States at 24 years old.

213
00:24:58,709 --> 00:25:00,973
Named after a car,
the Jensen Interceptor.

214
00:25:01,078 --> 00:25:03,512
A three-time local
speedway champion.

215
00:25:03,614 --> 00:25:06,913
You've done your homework.
Or do you just know everything?

216
00:25:07,018 --> 00:25:10,010
Jensen Interceptor.
I had one.

217
00:25:10,555 --> 00:25:12,716
Handled like
a school bus.

218
00:25:13,658 --> 00:25:16,627
Call me Coach.
Everyone does.

219
00:25:17,528 --> 00:25:19,189
Gunner. Lists.

220
00:25:20,998 --> 00:25:22,488
This is Frank.

221
00:25:23,668 --> 00:25:25,602
I'll show you around.

222
00:25:26,337 --> 00:25:28,305
We have a fully
functioning auto shop,

223
00:25:28,406 --> 00:25:30,567
just like you'd find
in the outside world.

224
00:25:30,675 --> 00:25:33,041
Each team has
their own shop.

225
00:25:33,144 --> 00:25:35,669
We don't help them.
They don't help us.

226
00:25:35,780 --> 00:25:38,681
To the inmates, you're Jensen Ames,
the new grease monkey.

227
00:25:38,783 --> 00:25:41,081
Nobody will know you're
Frank except us on the team

228
00:25:41,185 --> 00:25:42,174
and a handful
of the guards.

229
00:25:42,286 --> 00:25:43,310
Nobody will talk.

230
00:25:43,421 --> 00:25:44,888
How can you
be so sure?

231
00:25:44,989 --> 00:25:50,188
Hennessey. In here, she is
judge, jury and executioner.

232
00:25:50,661 --> 00:25:54,495
The race is her baby.
Anyone who threatens it, she kills.

233
00:25:54,599 --> 00:25:55,691
<i>The audience for</i>
<i>the race has halved</i>

234
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:56,824
<i>since Frank's been</i>
<i>out of the game,</i>

235
00:25:58,169 --> 00:25:59,636
<i>and so has the</i>
<i>corporation's profit.</i>

236
00:25:59,737 --> 00:26:01,762
<i>That's why she needs you.</i>

237
00:26:03,307 --> 00:26:05,002
What's back there?

238
00:26:06,077 --> 00:26:08,045
That's a good
question.

239
00:26:08,145 --> 00:26:12,104
Hennessey's had a whole wing of
the prison in isolation for a month.

240
00:26:12,216 --> 00:26:14,047
Working on
something.

241
00:26:14,652 --> 00:26:16,745
Time to meet
the Monster.

242
00:26:21,826 --> 00:26:24,056
Mustang V8 Fastback.

243
00:26:24,161 --> 00:26:27,096
Took the best
and made it better.

244
00:26:27,999 --> 00:26:31,992
That's a V8 Roush 5.4 liter
with a Ford Racing supercharger

245
00:26:32,103 --> 00:26:34,571
putting out 850
horsepower and close to...

246
00:26:34,672 --> 00:26:36,139
Seven hundred
pounds of torque

247
00:26:36,240 --> 00:26:39,368
with sequential
multi-port fuel injection.

248
00:26:39,477 --> 00:26:42,173
Looks like there's
a 250 hp NOS unit.

249
00:26:43,414 --> 00:26:44,904
Just in case.

250
00:26:47,618 --> 00:26:51,554
Then we had some fun customizing
your personal protection package.

251
00:26:51,656 --> 00:26:55,615
Three-quarter inch steel
plate, front and sides.

252
00:26:56,327 --> 00:27:00,320
Bulletproof glass will
be here, here and there.

253
00:27:00,431 --> 00:27:05,892
And in the rear, a six-inch
solid steel shield we call

254
00:27:08,139 --> 00:27:09,731
"the tombstone."

255
00:27:10,941 --> 00:27:15,742
Oil, smoke, and
napalm for defense.

256
00:27:16,247 --> 00:27:20,741
And twin 30-millimeter belt-fed
