We can beat him.

509
00:51:58,793 --> 00:52:00,260
Look out!

510
00:52:15,943 --> 00:52:20,573
<i>Grimm, Colt and Siad are gone.
Six remaining drivers alive.</i>

511
00:52:20,681 --> 00:52:22,979
<i>Subscribe to Stage 2 now!</i>

512
00:52:36,697 --> 00:52:40,133
We have 14 hours,
gentlemen, so let's get to work.

513
00:52:40,234 --> 00:52:41,997
Starting with this.

514
00:52:43,137 --> 00:52:45,162
So what happened
out there, Case?

515
00:52:45,272 --> 00:52:46,500
He got distracted.

516
00:52:46,607 --> 00:52:48,074
He got distracted?

517
00:52:58,919 --> 00:53:00,045
Coach!

518
00:53:00,154 --> 00:53:01,212
What?

519
00:53:01,322 --> 00:53:04,120
Look at this.
The oil sprayers work fine.

520
00:53:05,092 --> 00:53:06,957
Well, I'll
be damned.

521
00:53:16,280 --> 00:53:17,406
Stop.

522
00:53:25,038 --> 00:53:26,300
Last place.

523
00:53:26,773 --> 00:53:28,001
It's too bad.

524
00:53:30,777 --> 00:53:32,438
Look on the
bright side.

525
00:53:35,616 --> 00:53:37,481
Everyone loves
a comeback.

526
00:53:54,984 --> 00:53:57,009
What can I do for
you, Mr. Ames?

527
00:53:57,120 --> 00:53:58,815
You sure are lucky
a driver like me

528
00:53:58,922 --> 00:54:02,016
just happened to turn up
in your prison when I did.

529
00:54:02,125 --> 00:54:04,093
Oh, I'm more
than lucky.

530
00:54:04,928 --> 00:54:06,657
I'm blessed.

531
00:54:06,763 --> 00:54:08,594
Sometimes it's like
the right hand of God

532
00:54:08,698 --> 00:54:10,928
is sitting on
my shoulder.

533
00:54:13,970 --> 00:54:15,995
I'm not racing tomorrow.

534
00:54:17,473 --> 00:54:19,304
Go fuck yourself.

535
00:54:19,409 --> 00:54:20,603
Wait.

536
00:54:22,712 --> 00:54:24,612
Take his shackles off.

537
00:54:38,461 --> 00:54:40,656
Please excuse us,
Mr. Ulrich.

538
00:54:43,733 --> 00:54:45,997
And take Mr. James
with you.

539
00:54:58,448 --> 00:55:00,814
Do you recognize
these people?

540
00:55:01,651 --> 00:55:03,846
Because your
daughter will.

541
00:55:03,953 --> 00:55:05,944
They're her
new parents.

542
00:55:06,656 --> 00:55:08,351
What's her name?

543
00:55:09,025 --> 00:55:10,219
Piper.

544
00:55:11,594 --> 00:55:14,529
That's the man she'll
grow up calling Daddy.

545
00:55:16,366 --> 00:55:18,800
Unless you do
something about it.

546
00:55:20,837 --> 00:55:22,600
Where is she now?

547
00:55:22,705 --> 00:55:26,141
Oh, I'm sure I have her
address around here somewhere.

548
00:55:26,709 --> 00:55:28,973
You're a smart man,
Mr. Ames.

549
00:55:30,480 --> 00:55:33,005
Play my game, we both go home happy.

550
00:55:34,350 --> 00:55:37,478
The man who killed my
wife is in this prison.

551
00:55:38,888 --> 00:55:42,415
I wonder what he'll say
when I ask him why he did it.

552
00:55:42,525 --> 00:55:46,291
Why don't you look
in a mirror? Ask him.

553
00:55:47,964 --> 00:55:51,991
Poor Piper. It must be hard
growing up with that knowledge.

554
00:55:52,935 --> 00:55:55,563
That your father
killed your mother.

555
00:56:16,259 --> 00:56:18,056
You wanted a monster.

556
00:56:19,362 --> 00:56:21,159
Well, you've got one.

557
00:56:40,983 --> 00:56:42,780
She has your eyes.

558
00:56:46,656 --> 00:56:48,146
Her mother's.

559
00:56:49,625 --> 00:56:51,991
So why don't you wear
a number, Coach?

560
00:56:52,095 --> 00:56:54,256
Because I'm
not a prisoner.

561
00:56:54,364 --> 00:56:58,698
I qualified for parole
three years ago.

562
00:56:59,969 --> 00:57:02,096
Got as far
as the gate.

563
00:57:02,205 --> 00:57:05,766
They got a name for it,
something-or-other syndrome.

564
00:57:08,044 --> 00:57:12,242
The simple fact is, the world's
changed since I've been in here.

565
00:57:12,348 --> 00:57:15,647
Don't know it.
Don't much want to. But this?

566
00:57:17,186 --> 00:57:18,619
This I know.

567
00:57:18,721 --> 00:57:20,313
- What did they send you away for?
- Oh, plenty.

568
00:57:22,058 --> 00:57:23,491
And nothing.

569
00:57:24,227 --> 00:57:27,287
To what do we owe the
pleasure of your company?

570
00:57:28,364 --> 00:57:29,956
I killed my wife.

571
00:57:30,233 --> 00:57:31,359
Bullshit.

572
00:57:33,469 --> 00:57:36,461
You're a hard man, but
you ain't no wife killer.

573
00:57:36,572 --> 00:57:37,664
How do you know?

574
00:57:37,774 --> 00:57:39,264
I've met my share.

575
00:57:40,643 --> 00:57:43,237
But you, the way
you looked at her...

576
00:57:43,846 --> 00:57:47,304
You couldn't do that if
you'd killed her mother. So...

577
00:57:50,486 --> 00:57:52,181
I say bullshit.

578
00:57:55,224 --> 00:57:56,418
Coach.

579
00:58:00,430 --> 00:58:03,888
What would you say if I told
you Hennessey had my wife killed

580
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:04,989
and me framed for it

581
00:58:05,101 --> 00:58:08,468
so she could bring me in
here to be her Frankenstein?

582
00:58:08,571 --> 00:58:11,131
What would you say
to that bullshit?

583
00:58:16,746 --> 00:58:18,407
Her name was Suzy.

584
00:58:23,486 --> 00:58:24,475
I was always headed
here. Always knew.

585
00:58:27,123 --> 00:58:28,522
She didn't.

586
00:58:32,462 --> 00:58:34,987
She was my chance
at something else.

587
00:58:40,870 --> 00:58:43,532
And that bitch took
her away from me.

588
00:58:56,652 --> 00:59:00,019
"...that thy days may
be long upon the land

589
00:59:00,990 --> 00:59:04,187
"which the Lord thy...
Giveth thee.

590
00:59:29,385 --> 00:59:31,250
"Thou shalt not...

591
00:59:34,657 --> 00:59:35,988
"kill."

592
00:59:52,074 --> 00:59:55,271
You should take a break.
Get some sleep.

593
00:59:55,378 --> 00:59:57,005
I'm okay, Lists.

594
01:00:01,684 --> 01:00:03,276
Concentration
for the race.

595
01:00:03,386 --> 01:00:07,083
Concentration, that's what you need.
Gotta get your rest.

596
01:00:13,029 --> 01:00:14,826
Maybe you're right.

597
01:00:15,831 --> 01:00:18,231
I will take that
break after all.

598
01:00:23,940 --> 01:00:25,271
Good call.

599
01:00:26,309 --> 01:00:28,334
Guy can't grind
for shit.

600
01:00:54,236 --> 01:00:55,396
Move!

601
01:01:00,676 --> 01:01:02,268
Looking for me?

602
01:01:05,615 --> 01:01:06,946
Hold him.

603
01:01:16,993 --> 01:01:18,756
You killed my wife.

604
01:01:24,000 --> 01:01:25,865
Well, now, maybe I did.

605
01:01:28,270 --> 01:01:30,033
I don't care if
the queen bitch

606
01:01:30,139 --> 01:01:32,607
wants to save you
for the track.

607
01:01:32,708 --> 01:01:35,677
Nobody disrespects the
Brotherhood and lives.

608
01:01:37,580 --> 01:01:39,104
Put him down.

609
01:01:40,683 --> 01:01:42,947
I'm going to
take your head.

610
01:02:02,488 --> 01:02:04,183
What the fuck!

611
01:03:00,546 --> 01:03:03,208
Hennessey made me
do it. Ulrich...

612
01:03:05,184 --> 01:03:06,583
Ulrich too.

613
01:03:25,053 --> 01:03:26,611
Let me go, man.

614
01:03:30,659 --> 01:03:32,286
I'll do anything.

615
01:03:33,862 --> 01:03:35,921
You're going
to die here.

616
01:03:36,531 --> 01:03:37,793
Fuck you!

617
01:03:41,169 --> 01:03:43,034
Now, now, boys.

618
01:03:43,138 --> 01:03:45,629
Let's save that
for the track, huh?

619
01:04:09,998 --> 01:04:11,488
Coach!

620
01:04:11,600 --> 01:04:13,033
Take a look at this.

621
01:04:22,177 --> 01:04:24,975
What the hell were
they building in here?

622
01:04:28,516 --> 01:04:30,450
We'll find
out soon enough.

623
01:04:43,598 --> 01:04:44,929
Prisoner!

624
01:04:48,503 --> 01:04:50,437
It's time to get ready.

625
01:04:56,962 --> 01:05:00,398
<i>Welcome to the next
installment of Death Race.</i>

626
01:05:00,499 --> 01:05:02,160
<i>Stage 2 begins.</i>

627
01:05:02,934 --> 01:05:05,198
<i>Grimm, Colt and</i>
<i>Siad are gone.</i>

628
01:05:05,303 --> 01:05:07,396
<i>Six remaining drivers alive.</i>

629
01:05:07,506 --> 01:05:08,803
<i>14K.</i>

630
01:05:10,041 --> 01:05:11,338
<i>Pachenko.</i>

631
01:05:11,910 --> 01:05:13,207
<i>Riggins.</i>

632
01:05:14,079 --> 01:05:15,671
<i>Carson.</i>

633
01:05:15,780 --> 01:05:18,772
<i>Three-time winner</i>
<i>Machine Gun Joe.</i>

634
01:05:18,884 --> 01:05:23,184
<i>And starting from the back of the
grid, his archrival, Frankenstein.</i>

635
01:05:23,288 --> 01:05:26,451
<i>This could be the last time</i>
<i>we see Frankenstein race.</i>

636
01:05:26,558 --> 01:05:29,652
<i>Just one more victory</i>
<i>and he wins his freedom.</i>

637
01:05:29,761 --> 01:05:32,093
<i>If Joe doesn't</i>
<i>kill him first.</i>

638
01:05:33,865 --> 01:05:36,959
<i>Over 50 million viewers</i>
<i>have already subscribed.</i>

639
01:05:37,068 --> 01:05:41,368
<i>Don't miss this epic battle.</i>
<i>Subscribe to Stage 2, now.</i>

640
01:06:02,561 --> 01:06:04,051
Pay attention!

641
01:06:16,107 --> 01:06:17,506
Where is he?

642
01:06:21,146 --> 01:06:22,943
What are you doing?

643
01:06:25,684 --> 01:06:27,345
What's he doing?

644
01:06:30,889 --> 01:06:34,290
He's dropping back.
He's not even trying to race.

645
01:06:37,028 --> 01:06:38,586
We're gonna have
a little talk.

646
01:06:38,697 --> 01:06:42,064
We're gonna be done by the
time we leave the tunnel.

647
01:06:42,901 --> 01:06:45,267
Did you kill
the old Frank?

648
01:06:45,370 --> 01:06:46,598
What?

649
01:06:46,705 --> 01:06:48,434
Tunnel comes up fast.

650
01:06:49,207 --> 01:06:52,233
Remember what happened
to the napalm canister?

651
01:06:54,713 --> 01:06:57,580
Be a real shame for
that to happen to you.

652
01:07:01,920 --> 01:07:04,081
Did you kill
the old Frank?

653
01:07:06,658 --> 01:07:08,626
I sabotaged his
rear weapons.

654
01:07:08,727 --> 01:07:09,819
Why?

655
01:07:11,329 --> 01:07:12,387
Hennessey.

656
01:07:12,497 --> 01:07:16,160
She said she'd sign my release
papers. It's my life back.

657
01:07:16,701 --> 01:07:17,963
I'd have killed
him, too.

658
01:07:18,069 --> 01:07:19,468
I didn't kill him!

659
01:07:19,571 --> 01:07:22,563
He wouldn't quit. I just wanted
to make sure he didn't win.

660
01:07:22,674 --> 01:07:24,403
Why would Hennessey
want that?

661
01:07:24,509 --> 01:07:27,000
To keep Frank
here, racing.

662
01:07:29,514 --> 01:07:30,947
And yesterday?

663
01:07:31,049 --> 01:07:32,448
She wanted me
to set you back.

664
01:07:32,550 --> 01:07:35,280
So I'm not supposed
to win, either.

665
01:07:35,387 --> 01:07:37,878
Just make it exciting.

666
01:07:44,329 --> 01:07:46,520
That's all
I wanted to know.

667
01:07:49,134 --> 01:07:50,533
Hold tight.

668
01:08:07,419 --> 01:08:09,853
Come on!
Just come on through!

669
01:08:31,309 --> 01:08:32,503
Damn!

670
01:08:39,751 --> 01:08:41,810
He's going
after Pachenko.

671
01:09:18,022 --> 01:09:20,650
Sword and shield
ahead. Take defense.

672
01:09:21,326 --> 01:09:22,520
No.

673
01:09:24,896 --> 01:09:27,228
There's someone
I need to kill.

674
01:09:28,933 --> 01:09:30,525
You're out in front.

675
01:09:30,635 --> 01:09:32,193
Who are you going
to shoot at?

676
01:09:34,005 --> 01:09:35,802
You're a dead man!

677
01:09:41,246 --> 01:09:43,476
I told you to
take defense!

678
01:09:58,329 --> 01:10:00,422
He's too heavily
armored!

679
01:10:05,870 --> 01:10:07,098
Fuck!

680
01:10:09,007 --> 01:10:10,668
Hit the smoke.

681
01:11:00,258 --> 01:11:02,954
This is a race.
You don't go backwards.

682
01:11:12,871 --> 01:11:15,431
And you don't get
out of the car.

683
01:11:27,418 --> 01:11:29,818
It was Hennessey.
Hennessey.

684
01:11:29,921 --> 01:11:32,481
I know. She's next.

685
01:11:46,337 --> 01:11:49,033
I got it. Frank's
out of his car.

686
01:11:49,140 --> 01:11:50,471
What?

687
01:11:50,575 --> 01:11:51,872
He stepped out
of his car.

688
01:11:51,976 --> 01:11:53,841
Okay. I see him.
I need guns.

689
01:11:53,945 --> 01:11:56,436
Yes. Sword coming
up in 50 yards.

690
01:12:00,451 --> 01:12:01,816
What happened?
I don't know.

691
01:12:01,920 --> 01:12:03,444
Somebody must
have grabbed it.

692
01:12:03,554 --> 01:12:04,987
What do you mean,
somebody grabbed it?

693
01:12:05,089 --> 01:12:07,819
Look, man.
I thought it was lit.

694
01:12:07,926 --> 01:12:09,791
What do you mean,
you thought?

695
01:12:09,894 --> 01:12:11,725
Man, get the fuck
out of my car.

696
01:12:11,829 --> 01:12:12,955
What?

697
01:12:13,064 --> 01:12:15,624
I said, get the fuck
out of my car!

698
01:12:32,483 --> 01:12:33,916
Oh, hell, no!
Come on, man.

699
01:12:34,018 --> 01:12:36,612
Listen, we got...
Wait! Wait! Wait!

700
01:12:36,721 --> 01:12:39,212
Wait! Wait! It ain't my turn!
It's not what I do.

701
01:12:39,324 --> 01:12:40,757
Get in there.

702
01:12:43,061 --> 01:12:45,029
Don't let me
down, boy.

703
01:12:59,477 --> 01:13:01,445
Release the Dreadnought.

704
01:13:11,389 --> 01:13:12,686
Coach?

705
01:13:21,933 --> 01:13:23,025
Oh.

706
01:13:23,134 --> 01:13:26,194
Well, I guess we know
what she was building now.

707
01:13:34,145 --> 01:13:35,772
Activate weapons.

708
01:13:49,927 --> 01:13:51,394
Jesus Christ!

709
01:14:27,031 --> 01:14:28,362
Coach, any ideas?

710
01:14:28,466 --> 01:14:29,956
You just have to
tough it out, I guess.

711
01:14:30,068 --> 01:14:33,936
Hennessey will take it off after
she's pumped up the ratings.

712
01:14:37,041 --> 01:14:38,906
You sure
about that?

713
01:14:58,096 --> 01:14:59,723
Where the hell is
that thing going?

714
01:16:05,363 --> 01:16:06,694
Fuck me.

715
01:16:21,045 --> 01:16:22,342
<i>Lists.</i>

716
01:16:23,181 --> 01:16:24,148
Receiving.

717
01:16:24,248 --> 01:16:26,341
I want you to patch me
through to another car.

718
01:16:26,450 --> 01:16:27,644
On it.

719
01:16:33,658 --> 01:16:34,886
<i>Joe?</i>

720
01:16:35,893 --> 01:16:37,019
Who is this?

721
01:16:37,128 --> 01:16:38,959
It's Frank.
What do you want?

722
01:16:39,063 --> 01:16:41,531
How about we play
a little offense?

723
01:16:44,502 --> 01:16:46,367
I hope you know
what you're doing.

724
01:18:07,385 --> 01:18:09,410
Now that's entertainment!

725
01:18:10,454 --> 01:18:11,682
Damn it!

726
01:18:19,597 --> 01:18:23,727
Frankenstein!
Frankenstein! Frankenstein!

727
01:18:23,834 --> 01:18:27,361
Frankenstein! Frankenstein!

728
01:18:27,805 --> 01:18:29,739
Frankenstein! Frankenstein!

729
01:18:43,054 --> 01:18:45,113
Nice reflexes
there, Igor.

730
01:18:47,892 --> 01:18:49,689
Race car reflexes.

731
01:18:51,529 --> 01:18:53,258
You look lost, pal.

732
01:18:53,831 --> 01:18:55,389
Not this time.

733
01:18:57,068 --> 01:19:00,469
I got this feeling that
you and Frank are close.

734
01:19:01,872 --> 01:19:03,430
Real close.

735
01:19:03,541 --> 01:19:07,068
That weird accent.
You even kind of sound alike.

736
01:19:08,179 --> 01:19:11,740
I was wondering, what
if you got in a accident?

737
01:19:13,584 --> 01:19:16,747
Would that throw Frank
off his game a little bit?

738
01:19:17,288 --> 01:19:18,687
I doubt it,

739
01:19:19,123 --> 01:19:21,421
sick, fucked-up
guy that he is.

740
01:19:22,827 --> 01:19:25,193
He might just
want to kill you.

741
01:19:28,099 --> 01:19:29,589
That's cool.

742
01:19:31,335 --> 01:19:33,735
So I guess I'll
see him later.

743
01:19:34,839 --> 01:19:36,067
Right?

744
01:19:39,410 --> 01:19:40,843
Let's roll.

745
01:20:00,398 --> 01:20:04,027
Ma'am, with all respect,
what are we going to do?

746
01:20:04,135 --> 01:20:06,831
We're going to kill
him, of course.

747
01:20:06,937 --> 01:20:08,529
You want me to
kill Frankenstein?

748
01:20:08,639 --> 01:20:10,163
Don't be stupid.

749
01:20:10,274 --> 01:20:12,469
Frankenstein
can't die.

750
01:20:12,576 --> 01:20:14,737
After all,
he's just a mask.

751
01:20:42,506 --> 01:20:45,873
Tonight is the
final leg of the Death Race,

752
01:20:45,976 --> 01:20:49,468
and perhaps a new
champion will arise.

753
01:20:50,080 --> 01:20:51,843
A five times winner.

754
01:20:52,616 --> 01:20:56,450
The first man ever
to gain his freedom.

755
01:20:58,222 --> 01:21:02,454
The world gave you to me because
you were not fit to be a part of it.

756
01:21:03,027 --> 01:21:05,427
You were not fit
to be husbands,

757
01:21:06,397 --> 01:21:08,695
you were not fit
to be fathers,

758
01:21:09,900 --> 01:21:13,859
and were too dangerous to
live with the rest of us.

759
01:21:14,772 --> 01:21:16,706
What is this
shit, man?

760
01:21:17,508 --> 01:21:19,976
But when you race tonight,

761
01:21:20,077 --> 01:21:23,342
know that the eyes of
the world are upon you.

762
01:21:50,007 --> 01:21:53,875
And know that the very same
world which rejected you

763
01:21:53,978 --> 01:21:56,845
now lives and
breathes with you.

764
01:21:57,715 --> 01:22:01,481
And it draws inspiration
from your courage.

765
01:22:02,353 --> 01:22:04,287
No one is ever gonna
win five races.

766
01:22:04,388 --> 01:22:06,583
So race well...

767
01:22:06,690 --> 01:22:08,419
Nobody is ever
getting out of here.

768
01:22:08,526 --> 01:22:12,223
...and know that I
consider you all my heroes.

769
01:22:24,608 --> 01:22:26,803
I want to show
you something.

770
01:22:28,879 --> 01:22:32,315
<i>Can't kill me.</i>
<i>Can't kill me. I'm the fucking Reaper.</i>

771
01:22:36,420 --> 01:22:38,183
<i>You can burn me.</i>

772
01:22:38,789 --> 01:22:41,986
<i>You can shoot me.</i>
<i>But you can't motherfucking...</i>

773
01:22:42,092 --> 01:22:43,286
There.

774
01:22:58,709 --> 01:23:00,233
Gunner, Lists.

775
01:23:00,844 --> 01:23:02,311
Will Hennessey's
inspectors care

776
01:23:02,413 --> 01:23:04,506
if we had a half
gallon reserve tank?

777
01:23:04,615 --> 01:23:06,242
Another half gallon?

778
01:23:06,350 --> 01:23:08,784
You got a fuel tank
that holds 35 gallons.

779
01:23:08,886 --> 01:23:11,753
What the hell you want
another half gallon for?

780
01:23:11,855 --> 01:23:13,447
Coach?

781
01:23:13,557 --> 01:23:15,991
Let's give the man
what he wants.

782
01:23:19,029 --> 01:23:20,997
Hey, where are
you going?

783
01:23:28,072 --> 01:23:30,131
Oh, this is
not good.

784
01:23:44,922 --> 01:23:47,152
Real brave,
coming over here.

785
01:23:53,063 --> 01:23:57,022
I'm going to win this race,
'cause I want out of this shithole.

786
01:23:58,035 --> 01:24:00,435
I've already won
three races.

787
01:24:00,537 --> 01:24:04,268
Two more, and I'm
smoking Cohibas in Miami.

788
01:24:08,145 --> 01:24:10,943
Frank might want
to think about that.

789
01:24:11,048 --> 01:24:12,879
'Cause I'm gone.

790
01:24:13,584 --> 01:24:14,949
Out of here.

791
01:24:16,320 --> 01:24:18,288
Then maybe
it's his turn.

792
01:24:18,389 --> 01:24:21,415
Maybe he's thinking it's
the other way around.

793
01:24:26,130 --> 01:24:29,622
From here on out, you stay
the fuck out of my pit.

794
01:24:39,009 --> 01:24:40,101
Hey.

795
01:24:42,880 --> 01:24:45,974
Thinking you and Frank
should have a little talk.

796
01:24:49,787 --> 01:24:53,917
<i>Welcome to the final
installment of Death Race.</i>

797
01:24:54,692 --> 01:24:56,182
<i>Seven men dead.</i>

798
01:24:56,293 --> 01:24:57,590
<i>Siad,</i>

799
01:24:57,695 --> 01:24:59,219
<i>Grimm,</i>

800
01:24:59,329 --> 01:25:01,126
<i>Colt, Pachenko,</i>

801
01:25:01,832 --> 01:25:03,060
<i>Carson,</i>

802
01:25:03,167 --> 01:25:04,225
<i>Riggins</i>

803
01:25:04,334 --> 01:25:07,531
<i>and 14K are all dead.</i>

804
01:25:07,638 --> 01:25:10,971
<i>Just Frankenstein and</i>
<i>Machine Gun Joe survive.</i>

805
01:25:11,075 --> 01:25:13,475
<i>Frank, racing for</i>
<i>his freedom.</i>

806
01:25:13,577 --> 01:25:16,546
<i>Joe, doing anything</i>
<i>to stop him.</i>

807
01:25:16,647 --> 01:25:19,980
<i>It's mano y mano,
and there will be no mercy.</i>

808
01:25:20,084 --> 01:25:23,918
<i>Tonight, only one man will
walk off this track alive.</i>

809
01:25:24,021 --> 01:25:27,650
<i>A record 70 million are
already watching. Join them.</i>

810
01:25:27,758 --> 01:25:30,386
<i>Subscribe to the</i>
<i>final stage now.</i>

811
01:25:34,331 --> 01:25:36,162
It's an honor to navigate for you, sir.

812
01:25:36,266 --> 01:25:37,893
They call me...
Save it.

813
01:25:38,001 --> 01:25:40,663
We won't have time
to get acquainted.

814
01:25:43,407 --> 01:25:45,398
What the
hell are those?

815
01:25:46,009 --> 01:25:48,773
Model 7 Russian
states armory RPG's.

816
01:25:49,780 --> 01:25:53,079
Armor-piercing, self-arming,
accurate to 1,000 yards.

817
01:25:54,518 --> 01:25:56,486
That's what
I thought.

818
01:26:02,192 --> 01:26:04,160
Prisoner, step back.

819
01:26:14,738 --> 01:26:18,037
I thought maybe you could
use a little inspiration.

820
01:26:19,476 --> 01:26:21,273
Your release papers.

821
01:26:22,079 --> 01:26:24,206
They're already
signed.

822
01:26:24,314 --> 01:26:27,579
All you have to do is
walk off that track alive.

823
01:26:27,684 --> 01:26:30,380
Well, and win,
of course.

824
01:26:39,363 --> 01:26:41,354
But if you do win,

825
01:26:41,465 --> 01:26:44,161
I want you to think
about staying here.

826
01:26:44,902 --> 01:26:46,529
As Frankenstein.

827
01:26:47,571 --> 01:26:49,038
With me.

828
01:26:49,506 --> 01:26:50,700
Yeah.

829
01:26:52,309 --> 01:26:54,140
I can see the appeal.

830
01:26:55,479 --> 01:26:58,209
What would you do
with your freedom?

831
01:26:58,982 --> 01:27:00,677
Go back to
your daughter?

832
01:27:00,784 --> 01:27:02,149
That's the idea.

833
01:27:03,086 --> 01:27:04,553
The thing is,

834
01:27:04,655 --> 01:27:07,681
are you really the best
future she could possibly have?

835
01:27:09,726 --> 01:27:11,853
Are you really
daddy material?

836
01:27:11,962 --> 01:27:14,021
Or deep down, are
you something else?

837
01:27:19,970 --> 01:27:24,031
If you decided that out there on
that track is where you belong,

838
01:27:24,141 --> 01:27:29,078
it would be the most unselfish
act of love I've ever seen.

839
01:27:35,319 --> 01:27:37,583
Just something
to think about.

840
01:28:17,194 --> 01:28:18,684
What's this?

841
01:28:18,829 --> 01:28:20,524
Small modification.

842
01:28:21,798 --> 01:28:25,894
So Hennessey tells me if you're going
to win, I'm supposed to stop you.

843
01:28:26,003 --> 01:28:27,698
Oh, yeah?
Yeah.

844
01:28:29,673 --> 01:28:32,437
Sounds like the odds
are stacked against us.

845
01:28:32,542 --> 01:28:34,533
Then do what
you do best.

846
01:28:36,813 --> 01:28:38,041
Drive.

847
01:28:49,192 --> 01:28:52,423
Gentlemen, this should be interesting.

848
01:29:16,820 --> 01:29:18,310
Lit sword up ahead.

849
01:29:18,422 --> 01:29:20,287
Deactivate that.
Sir?

850
01:29:20,390 --> 01:29:21,857
Just do it.

851
01:29:23,293 --> 01:29:24,988
Switch it back on.

852
01:29:25,595 --> 01:29:27,256
Weapons are up!

853
01:29:27,664 --> 01:29:28,631
Damn it!

854
01:29:39,376 --> 01:29:40,468
Shit.

855
01:29:42,279 --> 01:29:43,871
Lit shield up ahead!

856
01:29:48,018 --> 01:29:49,007
Damn it!

857
01:29:49,119 --> 01:29:50,086
What happened?

858
01:29:50,187 --> 01:29:52,121
Hennessey must have
deactivated it. Bitch!

859
01:29:59,262 --> 01:30:00,627
Light me up.

860
01:30:07,437 --> 01:30:09,098
It's party time.

861
01:30:39,603 --> 01:30:41,833
Coach, we gotta
get the firepower.

862
01:30:41,938 --> 01:30:43,701
Nothing lit
for a half lap.

863
01:30:43,807 --> 01:30:45,866
We won't last that long!

864
01:31:23,647 --> 01:31:25,239
Drop the tombstone.

865
01:31:25,348 --> 01:31:26,406
What?

866
01:31:26,716 --> 01:31:27,876
Do it!

867
01:31:31,855 --> 01:31:33,914
On my mark. Three,

868
01:31:36,460 --> 01:31:37,518
two,

869
01:31:38,762 --> 01:31:39,888
one!

870
01:31:41,965 --> 01:31:43,091
Mark.

871
01:31:46,770 --> 01:31:48,067
Damn it!

872
01:31:49,306 --> 01:31:51,797
That shit don't
work twice, playboy!

873
01:31:58,915 --> 01:32:00,143
Shit.

874
01:32:00,250 --> 01:32:02,218
Lit shield in
quarter lap.

875
01:32:02,319 --> 01:32:04,219
Do you hear that?
Lit shield in the quarter lap.

876
01:32:19,870 --> 01:32:21,633
He's coming up fast.

877
01:32:22,806 --> 01:32:26,640
Let them get the shield.
Keep the viewers interested.

878
01:32:36,186 --> 01:32:38,677
Son of a bitch!
He got the shield!

879
01:32:44,628 --> 01:32:46,255
Arm the explosive.

880
01:32:47,063 --> 01:32:48,553
Just in case.

881
01:32:55,038 --> 01:32:56,266
Yo, Frankenfreak.

882
01:32:56,373 --> 01:32:58,102
This villager's
got a pitchfork,

883
01:32:58,208 --> 01:33:00,472
and it's headed
straight up your ass.

884
01:33:26,937 --> 01:33:28,768
What just happened?

885
01:33:34,744 --> 01:33:37,542
Yeah! Yeah, Frank!

886
01:33:39,349 --> 01:33:42,216
They're off the track.
They're escaping.

887
01:33:42,319 --> 01:33:43,786
They're headed
for the bridge.

888
01:33:43,887 --> 01:33:46,447
Their weapons.
Hit the kill switches.

889
01:33:49,159 --> 01:33:52,458
Seventy million viewers,
ma'am. They're all watching.

890
01:33:52,562 --> 01:33:53,586
Shut the webcast down.

891
01:33:53,697 --> 01:33:54,721
Shut it down!

892
01:33:54,831 --> 01:33:56,890
Shut the fucking
computers down now!

893
01:34:01,304 --> 01:34:02,965
Get out! Get out!
Get out! Now!

894
01:34:03,073 --> 01:34:04,301
Get out! Get out!

895
01:34:04,407 --> 01:34:05,567
Get out! Get out!

896
01:34:11,081 --> 01:34:12,946
Yo, Frankenstein.

897
01:34:13,049 --> 01:34:14,983
<i>It's good we had</i>
<i>that little talk.</i>

898
01:34:18,188 --> 01:34:20,782
We gave that bitch
a good show, huh?

899
01:34:27,030 --> 01:34:28,520
Give me that!

900
01:34:28,965 --> 01:34:32,526
Okay, cocksucker,
fuck with me,

901
01:34:32,636 --> 01:34:34,604
and we'll see who
shits on the sidewalk.

902
01:34:38,875 --> 01:34:40,706
Somebody's mad
right now.

903
01:34:40,810 --> 01:34:43,040
Nobody fucks
with my car.

904
01:34:45,248 --> 01:34:46,613
Son of a bitch!

905
01:34:46,716 --> 01:34:47,944
Get the choppers
in the air!

906
01:34:48,551 --> 01:34:51,179
Come on. Off the ground. Go, go, go!

907
01:35:09,739 --> 01:35:11,263
So what's your
real name?

908
01:35:11,374 --> 01:35:13,433
I don't have the
time for small talk.

909
01:35:13,543 --> 01:35:15,977
Just want to know
who I'm riding with.

910
01:35:19,415 --> 01:35:21,906
Jensen Ames.

911
01:35:23,553 --> 01:35:25,384
Like...
Like the car.

912
01:35:25,488 --> 01:35:26,580
Like the car.

913
01:35:28,124 --> 01:35:31,287
Well, Jensen Ames,
I hope you got a plan,

914
01:35:31,461 --> 01:35:33,520
'cause it's not like we're
going to get very far.

915
01:35:33,630 --> 01:35:34,824
You're right.

916
01:35:35,498 --> 01:35:36,465
We won't.

917
01:35:45,624 --> 01:35:47,717
Now would be
a good time.

918
01:36:08,180 --> 01:36:10,080
Very nice modification.

919
01:36:12,818 --> 01:36:14,877
<i>That extra half</i>
<i>gallon reserve tank</i>

920
01:36:14,987 --> 01:36:17,012
<i>should see you through</i>
<i>to the finish.</i>

921
01:36:17,623 --> 01:36:20,217
<i>Bon voyage,</i> Frank.

922
01:36:52,525 --> 01:36:54,459
Choppers have
a visual, ma'am.

923
01:37:06,972 --> 01:37:08,599
Good luck, Joe.

924
01:37:25,257 --> 01:37:28,590
Get me a pilot.
I need to talk to a pilot right now.

925
01:37:29,061 --> 01:37:30,187
Okay. You're on.

926
01:37:30,296 --> 01:37:31,729
Stay with Frankenstein!
Don't lose him.

927
01:37:40,573 --> 01:37:41,972
Sure you're
up for this?

928
01:37:42,074 --> 01:37:43,132
I'm sure.

929
01:37:43,242 --> 01:37:44,539
I owe it to Frank.

930
01:37:44,643 --> 01:37:47,339
Besides, Hennessey already
gave me my release papers.

931
01:37:47,446 --> 01:37:49,573
They have to let me out.

932
01:39:00,319 --> 01:39:02,480
They've stopped
him, ma'am.

933
01:39:35,821 --> 01:39:38,051
<i>Keep your hands</i>
<i>where we can see them.</i>

934
01:39:38,157 --> 01:39:40,250
<i>You are under arrest!</i>

935
01:39:40,359 --> 01:39:44,125
<i>I repeat, keep your hands</i>
<i>where we can see them!</i>

936
01:39:44,230 --> 01:39:46,164
<i>You are under arrest!</i>

937
01:39:51,670 --> 01:39:54,537
Hey, Igor.
Merry Christmas.

938
01:40:04,216 --> 01:40:06,548
Come on. Let's
get out of here.

939
01:40:30,576 --> 01:40:31,702
Nice.

940
01:40:33,212 --> 01:40:34,702
The fact you have
duds like these

941
01:40:34,813 --> 01:40:36,246
might make someone
question your...

942
01:40:36,348 --> 01:40:37,372
My taste?

943
01:40:37,483 --> 01:40:38,745
Yeah. So to speak.

944
01:40:38,851 --> 01:40:40,910
I don't know about you,
but I'm headed to Miami.

945
01:40:41,020 --> 01:40:42,647
Miami's good.

946
01:40:43,555 --> 01:40:45,523
I'll meet you
down there.

947
01:40:46,792 --> 01:40:48,851
Once I got my baby girl.

948
01:40:55,901 --> 01:40:58,495
It's a shame I didn't get to
take care of that bitch Hennessey.

949
01:40:58,604 --> 01:41:01,232
Yeah. That is a shame.

950
01:41:13,218 --> 01:41:14,810
Frankenstein has
been retrieved.

951
01:41:14,920 --> 01:41:17,980
And, ma'am, ratings
are off the charts.

952
01:41:19,058 --> 01:41:22,221
Gifts and congratulations
are already coming in.

953
01:41:24,229 --> 01:41:25,821
You win again.

954
01:41:26,332 --> 01:41:27,799
Mr. Ulrich,

955
01:41:30,002 --> 01:41:31,629
I always win.

956
01:41:34,139 --> 01:41:35,401
Damn.

957
01:41:43,215 --> 01:41:44,842
I love this game.

958
01:42:15,447 --> 01:42:17,472
So we had to fix this car?

959
01:42:18,183 --> 01:42:20,413
How many times we gonna
keep doing this, man?

960
01:42:20,519 --> 01:42:22,453
This car is not
gonna start.

961
01:42:26,091 --> 01:42:27,183
Damn it!

962
01:42:27,626 --> 01:42:30,459
You say you want me to live
the life of an honest man, huh?

963
01:42:30,562 --> 01:42:32,962
Yep. You better
get used to it.

964
01:42:38,904 --> 01:42:39,996
Hey, Igor.

965
01:42:44,593 --> 01:42:45,924
Think we got
a little company.

966
01:43:29,104 --> 01:43:30,093
What took you so long?

967
01:43:30,205 --> 01:43:32,366
Had trouble getting my
release papers approved.

968
01:43:32,474 --> 01:43:35,466
Wait here. There's
someone I want you to meet.

969
01:43:39,581 --> 01:43:41,276
Look at her.

970
01:43:42,317 --> 01:43:43,978
She has beautiful eyes.

971
01:43:44,119 --> 01:43:45,518
They're her mother's.

972
01:43:45,620 --> 01:43:47,417
Where'd you get the rims?

973
01:43:47,522 --> 01:43:49,422
I won it.
Card game.

974
01:43:49,858 --> 01:43:50,847
Yeah, right.

975
01:43:50,959 --> 01:43:52,017
No, really.

976
01:43:52,327 --> 01:43:53,988
How many horsepower's in this engine?

977
01:43:54,095 --> 01:43:55,824
Five hundred.

978
01:43:56,631 --> 01:43:57,996
You sure
about that?

979
01:43:58,133 --> 01:43:59,794
<i>Someone</i>
<i>once asked me,</i>

980
01:43:59,935 --> 01:44:02,529
<i>did I think I was the best
future for my little girl?</i>

981
01:44:03,872 --> 01:44:06,306
<i>Something I've thought</i>
<i>about for a long time.</i>

982
01:44:07,042 --> 01:44:08,703
<i>This is what I decided.</i>

983
01:44:09,845 --> 01:44:13,440
<i>No one in this world is perfect.
Heaven knows I'm not.</i>

984
01:44:15,083 --> 01:44:18,484
<i>But I love her more than</i>
<i>anyone else possibly could.</i>

985
01:44:19,054 --> 01:44:22,387
<i>In the end, that's</i>
<i>all that matters.</i>

986
01:44:22,491 --> 01:44:26,689
<i>She's my chance at something else.</i>
<i>Something better.</i>

987
01:44:26,795 --> 01:44:29,491
<i>And there's no way</i>
<i>I'm letting go of that.</i>

988
01:50:26,738 --> 01:50:30,765
<i>Okay, cocksucker, fuck with me,</i>

989
01:50:30,875 --> 01:50:32,900
<i>and we'll see who</i>
<i>shits on the sidewalk.</i>

990
01:52:32,901 --> 01:52:33,901
Subtitles by LeapinLar
